body:
uploaded index.html and LOGO.GIF. The HTML asks
for logo.gif. It works when I open the page on my old Windows machine,
but the server shows a broken picture. Have I worn the GIF out?

Tested with a copy and found the client changing the endings in text
mode. Binary preserved the file I wanted. Also checked my GIF uploads;
they were already binary, so one mystery at a time.

Files you explicitly saved to disk remain there without a phone
connection. A page in a browser is not necessarily saved permanently;
use the browser's save option if you need a copy.

Teh stream and game share teh link. Stop teh stream for a comparison;
choosing a low audio rate does not make its traffic disappear. You need
room for game packets rather than using teh whole line continuously.
